ey, showed a 6-point race, so a blue-wave environment keeps this from being Safe R, but Conroy remains a clear underdog.", "watch": "A strong national Democratic wave or late outside spending against Baumgartner could tighten the race toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Michael Baumgartner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Republican Michael Baumgartner seeks a second term in Washington's 5th District, an R+5 seat centered on Spokane, in a rematch against Democrat Carmela Conroy. Baumgartner holds a decisive financial edge, having raised $2.2 million to Conroy's $723,000, and enters with the benefits of incumbency. Every major expert rater places the race on the Republican side, ranging from Solid R to Lean R, and prediction markets give Conroy only about a 15 percent chance.\n\nThe main Democratic hope is the national environment, which leans favorable this cycle, and a May Democratic-sponsored poll showed a single-digit race. Still, with no recent independent polling and the district's partisan lean, Baumgartner is favored to hold the seat, with Conroy needing a substantial wave to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0968, "margin": -8.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1087, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0951, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0945, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1116, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0732, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1005, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.124, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1258, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1286, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.127, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1239, "margin": -8.0}, {"date